Description: pvr: make all multiview occlusion queries available
 With multiview, a query uses N consecutive query indices starting at the
 given query, N being the number of views in the view mask (Vulkan spec,
 Queries, "Query Operation"). pvr_occlusion_query_begin() added the first
 index N times to the list of the render, so only that index was marked
 available. The counters themselves are fine: all views write to the visreg
 of the first index and the per-view fragment jobs add up there
 (dEQP-VK.multiview.queries_and_timestamps.cmd_copy_query_pool_results.5_10_5_10
 passes). vkGetQueryPoolResults with VK_QUERY_RESULT_WAIT_BIT then waited
 for the remaining indices until the timeout and returned early, which fails
 dEQP-VK.multiview.*queries_and_timestamps.get_query_pool_results.5_10_5_10.
 .
 Add query + i for each view, so the other indices become available with a
 result of zero, as the spec allows.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
Author: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Generated-by: LLM
